  "title": "The Alon-Tarsi basis conjecture",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture If $B_1,B_2,\\ldots B_p$ are invertible $n \\times n$ matrices with entries in ${\\mathbb Z}_p$ for a prime $p$, then there is a $n \\times (p-1)n$ submatrix $A$ of $[B_1 B_2 \\ldots B_p]$ so that $A$ is an AT-base.",
